  "title": "The Memory Cloud Weather Report",
  "family": "fiction",
  "category": "fantasy and science fiction",
  "premise": "A cloud archivist wants to retrieve one happy picnic memory from a fantasy sky cabinet, but all the cloud drawers look identical. They sort the clouds by the objects visible inside instead of by cloud shape, find the red picnic kite, and label the drawer with that distinctive detail.",
  "hook": "The forecast says scattered memories.",
  "visible_action": "Cloud drawers drift; blurred mini-scenes swirl; archivist spots cup, umbrella, and kite icons; one drawer opens to an original picnic tableau.",
